<title>INDIA: India Andhra Bank lends 3-month money at 10.25 pct.</title>
<headline>India Andhra Bank lends 3-month money at 10.25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Andhra Bank said on Tuesday it concluded a deal in three-month interbank term market at 10.25 percent.</p>
<p>A bank official said it was a lender in the transaction.</p>
<p>He said the bank was quoting the following offer rates for</p>
<p>different maturities.</p>
<p>--.</p>
<p>    No of days			 Bid/offer</p>
<p>    ----------			-----------</p>
<p>    30 days			   ----/7.00</p>
<p>    60 days			   ----/8.50</p>
<p>    90 days			   ----/10.25</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>--- Bombay newsroom +91 22 265 9000</p>
</text>
